e,"_score_insider_own":74.7,"_gate_insider_buying":1.0,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Biohaven Ltd., a biopharmaceutical company, focuses on the discovery, development, and commercialization of treatments for immunology, neuroscience, and oncology therapeutic areas worldwide. It develops BHV-1300, which is in Phase 2 clinical trial to treat Graves' disease and rheumatoid arthritis; BHV-1400 that is in Phase 2 clinical trial for treating IgA nephropathy; BHV-1600, which is in Phase 1 clinical trial for the treatment of peripartum cardiomyopathy; BHV-8000 that is in Phase 3 clinical trial for treating Parkinson's disease; Opakalim, which is in Phase 3 clinical trial for the treatment of focal epilepsy; BHV-2100 that is in Phase 2 clinical trial for the treatment of pain disorders; and BHV-2000, which is in Phase 2 clinical trial for treating obesity. The company is also developing BHV-1510 that is in Phase 2 clinical trial for the treatment of advanced or metastatic epithelial tumors; and BHV-1530, which is in Phase 2 clinical trial for treating urothelial cancer and other tumors. In addition, its preclinical product pipeline includes BHV-1310 for treating myasthenia gravis; BHV-1320 for treating immune mediated-diseases; BHV-1450 for treating Pemphigus, MuSK MG, and LGI-1 Encephalitis; BHV-1420 for treating membranous nephropathy; BHV-1440 for treating Graves' disease and TED; BHV-6500 for treating type 1 diabetes; BHV-1490 for treating IgM neuropathy and Waldenstrom's; BHV-8100 for treating neurodegenerative diseases; and BHV-1955 for treating tinnitus. The company was formerly known as Biohaven Research Ltd. and changed its name to Biohaven Ltd. in September 2022. Biohaven Ltd. was incorporated in 2022 and is headquartered in New Haven, Connecticut.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Vladimir  Coric M.D. | Chairman & CEO | Age 54 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 274 people. Stock-based compensation of $410K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Biohaven Ltd. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $2.2B market cap.","Returns on capital run at -750% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $610M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at -28.7% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -3450.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 8.6% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-8.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Healthcare peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 130% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Large open-market insider purchases (net $33.1M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Research Analysts\u2019 Recent Ratings Changes for Biohaven (BHVN)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/research-analysts-recent-ratings-changes-for-biohaven-bhvn-2.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793870850.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.077,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Biohaven (BHVN) Could Be 64% Undervalued After Smaller Loss And BHV 1420 Data","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nyse-bhvn/biohaven/news/biohaven-bhvn-could-be-64-undervalued-after-smaller-loss-and","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793582867.468,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.863,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"The Technical Signals Behind (BHVN) That Institutions Follow","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/98/The_Technical_Signals_Behind_BHVN_That_Institutions_Follow_103126042401_1793435041.html","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793435041.0